C.7 Common-function evidence

The common-function assumption $m_\Pi = m_\Omega$ is not merely stated; it must be supported by direct evidence where such evidence exists. The protocol must report:

· whether the same rule has been implemented in two environments differing in the contested structural feature;
· the estimated effect difference;
· whether the difference is consistent with $\Lambda = 0$.

If no such evidence exists, the assumption is stated as an assumption and $\Lambda$ is reported as unmeasured.

